NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Crow does not distribute any NVIDIA file. No package of this project contains
one.

The CUDA backend is built against NVIDIA's CUDA Toolkit (version 13.3 on the
development machine) and needs NVIDIA's libraries at runtime. The installers
(CrowSetup; install.ps1 for the Windows cuBLAS files) download them at install time from NVIDIA's own PyPI wheels and puts
them next to the binaries that import them:

  - cublas64_13.dll and cublasLt64_13.dll in bin/ on Windows, and
    libcublas.so.13 and libcublasLt.so.13 in cuda/lib/ on Linux, from
    nvidia-cublas 13.6.0.2;
  - on Linux also libcudart.so.13 in cuda/lib/, from nvidia-cuda-runtime
    13.3.29, for sd-server;
  - for the crow-nest engine, NVRTC from nvidia-cuda-nvrtc 13.3.33.

They are NVIDIA's files, unmodified, under NVIDIA's own licence
(https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/index.html), which the user accepts there
when downloading them from NVIDIA. They are NOT covered by the MIT grant above.


